{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0130"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge history/modern-history","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/history__modern-history.g4.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",526],["-","They"],["+","Beyond"],["=",1],["-","defeated"],["+","the"],["=",1],["+","Drakensberg they met "],["=",4],["+","kingdom, which Shaka (c. 1787–1828) had forged between 1816 and 1828 from a small clan into the dominant power of the region, with disciplined regiments and the short stabbing spear; his reign coincided with the wars and migrations remembered as the Mfecane. Shaka had been murdered in 1828 by his half-brother Dingane, and it was Dingane's "],["=",2],["+","that the Voortrekkers defeated "],["=",82],["+","meant that the lands that make up today's South Africa experienced both a diamond fever and a gold rush within two decades; Johannesburg grew from a mining camp into the largest city in the region. The finds "],["=",310],["+","1816–1828 | Shaka rules the Zulu kingdom |\n| "],["=",18],["+","1867, 1886 | Diamonds at Kimberley, gold on the Witwatersrand |\n| "],["=",91]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",474],["-","Sie"],["+","Jenseits"],["=",1],["+","der Drakensberge trafen sie auf das Zulureich, das Shaka (um 1787–1828) zwischen 1816 und 1828 aus einem kleinen Clan zur beherrschenden Macht der Region geschmiedet hatte, mit disziplinierten Regimentern und dem kurzen Stoßspeer; seine Herrschaft fiel in die Zeit der Kriege und Wanderungen, die als Mfecane in Erinnerung sind. Shaka war 1828 von seinem Halbbruder Dingane ermordet worden, und Dinganes Heer "],["=",2],["+","die Voortrekker "],["=",8],["-","das Zulu-Heer "],["=",62],["+","bedeuteten, dass die Gebiete des heutigen Südafrika binnen zwei Jahrzehnten sowohl ein Diamantenfieber als auch einen Goldrausch erlebten; Johannesburg wuchs von einem Bergbaulager zur größten Stadt der Region. Die Funde "],["=",304],["+","1816–1828 | Shaka herrscht über das Zulureich |\n| "],["=",16],["+","1867, 1886 | Diamanten bei Kimberley, Gold am Witwatersrand |\n| "],["=",89]]}]},
